// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Object Size Filter";
export const html = "<h1>Object Size Filter</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>Within a fixed field of view, objects of the same type are usually a fairly consistent size. Or, when the field of view is narrow and the distance is short, objects near the top and bottom of the frame are detected at a size that increases or decreases along a consistent ratio.</p>\n      <p>Using this property, you can exclude a detected object from triggering an event when its size is much larger or smaller than expected.</p>\n\n      <h2>Minimum Size Filter</h2>\n      <p>The minimum size filter only recognizes a detected object when its bounding box is larger than the configured box. Open it from the sidebar under <strong>Video Input &rsaquo; Detection Filter</strong>, then select <strong>Min Size Filter</strong> in the main area.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\">\n      <div class=\"app-window\">\n        <div class=\"app-body\" style=\"min-height:auto;\">\n          <div class=\"app-sidebar-nav\" style=\"width:170px;\">\n            <div class=\"grp\">Video</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Video Input &#9662;</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Video Stream</div>\n            <div class=\"item active\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Detection Filter</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Output &#9656;</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"app-main\">\n            <div class=\"app-breadcrumb\">Home / Video Input / Detection Filter</div>\n            <div class=\"app-h\">Detection Filter</div>\n            <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px;\">\n              <span class=\"btn small primary\">Min Size Filter</span><span class=\"btn small\">Max Size Filter</span><span class=\"btn small\">Exclusion Area</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"app-panel\"><strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Min Size Filter &#9432;</strong></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption>Video Input &rarr; Detection Filter &rarr; Min Size Filter</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2>How the Minimum Size Filter Is Applied</h2>\n      <div class=\"figure\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 240\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(30,20)\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n      <text x=\"4\" y=\"-6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#23262f\" font-weight=\"700\">Object</text>\n      <rect x=\"-25\" y=\"-8\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f9e6e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"-23\" y=\"-14\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2f9e6e\" font-weight=\"700\">Min Size Filter</text>\n      <rect x=\"180\" y=\"220\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\"/>\n    </g>\n    <rect x=\"30\" y=\"196\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fde3e3\"/>\n    <text x=\"105\" y=\"213\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#c0392b\" font-weight=\"700\">Not Filtered!</text>\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(290,20)\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n      <text x=\"4\" y=\"-6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#23262f\" font-weight=\"700\">Object</text>\n      <rect x=\"35\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f9e6e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"37\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2f9e6e\" font-weight=\"700\">Min Size Filter</text>\n      <rect x=\"180\" y=\"220\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\"/>\n    </g>\n    <rect x=\"290\" y=\"196\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fde3e3\"/>\n    <text x=\"365\" y=\"213\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#c0392b\" font-weight=\"700\">Not Filtered!</text>\n\n    <g transform=\"translate(550,20)\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n      <text x=\"4\" y=\"-6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#23262f\" font-weight=\"700\">Object</text>\n      <rect x=\"5\" y=\"5\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f9e6e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"7\" y=\"-1\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2f9e6e\" font-weight=\"700\">Min Size Filter</text>\n      <rect x=\"180\" y=\"220\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\"/>\n    </g>\n    <rect x=\"550\" y=\"196\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e2f4e8\"/>\n    <text x=\"625\" y=\"213\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#20603a\" font-weight=\"700\">Filtered!</text>\n\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption>How the minimum size filter is applied</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>If the object's bounding box is larger than the minimum size filter box in either width or height, the object is not filtered. An object is only filtered out \u2014 and disappears \u2014 when its bounding box fits entirely inside the minimum size filter box. See the figure above for how filtering depends on the relative size of the filter box and the object's bounding box.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n        <p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Note</p>\n        <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">The Fire Detection application does not apply the minimum object size filter.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin:0;\">The Fall Detection application does not apply the minimum object size filter.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2>Maximum Size Filter</h2>\n      <p>The maximum size filter only recognizes a detected object when its bounding box is smaller than the configured box. Open it from the sidebar under <strong>Video Input &rsaquo; Detection Filter</strong>, then select <strong>Max Size Filter</strong> in the main area.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\">\n      <div class=\"app-window\">\n        <div class=\"app-body\" style=\"min-height:auto;\">\n          <div class=\"app-sidebar-nav\" style=\"width:170px;\">\n            <div class=\"grp\">Video</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Video Input &#9662;</div>\n            <div class=\"item\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Video Stream</div>\n            <div class=\"item active\" style=\"padding-left:26px;\">Detection Filter</div>\n            <div class=\"item\">Output &#9656;</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"app-main\">\n            <div class=\"app-breadcrumb\">Home / Video Input / Detection Filter</div>\n            <div class=\"app-h\">Detection Filter</div>\n            <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px;\">\n              <span class=\"btn small\">Min Size Filter</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">Max Size Filter</span><span class=\"btn small\">Exclusion Area</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"app-panel\"><strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Max Size Filter &#9432;</strong></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <figcaption>Video Input &rarr; Detection Filter &rarr; Max Size Filter</figcaption>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2>How the Maximum Size Filter Is Applied</h2>\n      <p>If the object's bounding box is larger than the maximum size filter box in either width or height, the object is filtered out. An object is only kept when its bounding box fits entirely inside the maximum size filter box. See the diagram above (with the comparison reversed) for how filtering depends on the relative size of the filter box and the object's bounding box.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n        <p style=\"margin:0;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Note</p>\n        <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0;\">The Fire Detection application does not apply the maximum object size filter.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2>How to Configure the Filter</h2>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Select the channel you want to configure the minimum size filter for.</li>\n        <li>Select the filter mode to apply to the minimum size filter.</li>\n        <li>Drag inside the filter area to move the filter's position.</li>\n        <li>Drag from a corner handle of the filter box to resize it.</li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h2>Filter Modes</h2>\n      <ul class=\"steps\">\n        <li><strong>Not Used</strong> &ndash; does not apply the minimum size filter to this channel.</li>\n        <li><strong>Normal</strong> &ndash; applies a single minimum size filter box.\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>Generally used when the field of view is distant and objects across the frame are a fairly similar size.</li>\n            <li>Configure a single box, and any object smaller than that box is filtered out.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>Advanced</strong> &ndash; configures two boxes based on perspective.\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>The near box should be set smaller than the size of objects near the bottom of the frame (closer to the camera).</li>\n            <li>The far box should be set smaller than the size of objects near the top of the frame (farther from the camera).</li>\n            <li>A minimum size filter box is calculated for each region of the frame at a ratio interpolated between the near and far boxes.</li>\n            <li>This applies a perspective-aware minimum size filter depending on where the object appears in the frame.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Saving, Loading, and Resetting Settings</h2>\n      <p>Click the button at the bottom of the screen to save the position and size of the filter you've configured for the video area.</p>\n      <p>Click the corresponding button to load the last saved filter settings for the selected channel.</p>\n      <p>Click the button at the bottom left to clear and reset the filter settings for the selected channel.</p>";
